window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-fc9cd7880ec6ce59"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"_1\">发布与分享</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>发布网站之前先检查网站，然后选择允许哪些人访问，以及允许哪些人协助编辑。</p> <p><a id=\"review-and-share-your-site\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">分享前检查</h2> <p>分享网站之前：</p> <ol> <li> <h3 id=\"_3\">试用网站</h3> </li> <li>检查网站内容、生成的文本和图片、链接、上传文件、表单以及交互行为。</li> <li>按照目标访客的使用方式测试网站，包括访问和登录行为。</li> </ol> <p>如果网站由本地项目构建，还要在 Codex <a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">审查面板</a>中检查源代码更改和数据库迁移。</p> <ol> <li> <h3 id=\"_4\">检查数据和访问权限</h3> </li> <li>确认网站没有泄露机密或敏感信息、秘密值，或你无权分享的第三方内容。</li> <li>检查会收集个人信息或其他访客内容的功能，决定网站是否应该收集、分享或发布这些信息。</li> <li>如果网站使用 Sign in with ChatGPT，请说明网站会收到哪些访客信息，以及如何使用这些信息。</li> <li> <p>如果网站收集或处理个人数据，请遵守<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001340\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">适用的隐私和数据保护法律（需联网）</a>。</p> </li> <li> <h3 id=\"_5\">选择受众</h3> </li> <li>选择适合目标受众的最小共享范围。</li> <li>打开共享的网站，确认目标受众可以访问。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"control-access-and-secrets\"></a></p> <p>在检查网站内容、数据处理方式和预期受众期间，请限制访问范围。</p> <p>请使用网站提供的共享选项来选择访客。访客访问权限允许对方打开网站，但不代表对方可以编辑网站。</p> <p>如果采用限人分享，受邀访客必须使用收到访问权限的账户登录。公开网站无需 ChatGPT 工作区访问权限即可访问。网站的受众范围设置和网站内置的登录功能是彼此独立的控制项。</p> <p>有关共享控制项和网站管理说明，请参阅帮助中心的<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001339\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">创建和管理 ChatGPT 网站（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"update-your-site\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">发布更新</h2> <p>在 ChatGPT 中打开网站，并描述你想做的更改。检查结果、保存一个版本，然后部署。最后在已发布的 URL 上检查更改。</p> <p>检查网站代码，以及网站保存或展示的任何数据。使用目标受众中的账户测试已发布的网站。</p> <h2 id=\"_7\">选择谁可以访问</h2> <p>新网站最初只对所有者和工作区管理员开放，除非你更改访问权限。根据账户和工作区设置，共享选项可能包括：</p> <ul> <li><strong>所有者和工作区管理员</strong></li> <li><strong>选定的活跃用户或群组</strong>（若支持）</li> <li><strong>受邀的外部访客</strong>（开放外部邀请时）</li> <li><strong>工作区中的任何人</strong>（若支持）</li> <li><strong>互联网上的任何人</strong>（仅在启用公开发布后）</li> </ul> <p>在 Enterprise 工作区中，默认关闭公开发布。管理员必须先启用该功能，符合条件的成员才能公开发布。访客访问权限允许对方打开网站，但不代表对方可以编辑。<a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df?anchor=enable-sites-and-permissions\">查看 Sites 管理指南</a>。</p> <p>例如，你可以这样提出请求：</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">先向我展示当前网站并确认其 URL，然后将网站访问权限更改为工作区内所有人。\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"_8\">邀请工作区外的人员</h2> <p>外部邀请可以让你在不公开网站的情况下，与指定访客分享网站。你可以邀请工作区外的人员，也可以通过个人账户分享私人网站。</p> <p>外部邀请功能正逐步向使用 Sites 的 Plus、Pro、Business 和 Enterprise 方案用户推出。如果看不到邀请选项，请检查当前选定的账户、网站所有权、工作区权限，以及该功能是否已向你的账户开放。</p> <ol> <li>打开一个你拥有的网站，然后选择 <strong>Share（分享）</strong>。</li> <li>如果要保持网站私密，请将 <strong>Who has access（谁可以访问）</strong>设置为 <strong>Only those invited（仅限受邀人员）</strong>。</li> <li>在 <strong>Search for people or groups（搜索人员或群组）</strong>下输入访客的电子邮件地址；对于个人网站，选择 <strong>Enter an email address（输入电子邮件地址）</strong>，然后选择收件人。</li> <li>检查受众范围和收件人的 <strong>Viewer（访客）</strong>权限，然后选择 <strong>Invite（邀请）</strong>。</li> <li>确认访客显示在已保存的访问列表中。分享网站链接，并请对方使用收到邀请的账户登录。</li> </ol> <p>外部访客可以打开和使用网站，但不会成为工作区成员或网站编辑者，也无法编辑或发布网站。邀请只授予对该网站的访问权限；分享前仍要检查网站内容和已连接的数据。</p> <p>在 Enterprise 中，管理员可以在 <strong>Workspace settings（工作区设置）&gt; Permissions &amp; roles（权限和角色）</strong>下管理 <strong>Allow members to invite external visitors to sites（允许成员邀请外部访客访问 Sites）</strong>。此权限与公开发布网站的权限相互独立。Business 工作区没有单独的外部邀请开关；必须启用 Sites，且该账户必须能够使用此功能。</p> <p>要移除访客，请打开网站共享控制项并移除其访问权限。还要检查剩余的受众设置：移除某一项邀请，并不会撤销此人通过公开分享、工作区分享或群组分享获得的访问权限。</p> <h2 id=\"_9\">协作编辑网站</h2> <p>网站协作需要工作区。该功能开放后，网站所有者可以邀请同一工作区中的活跃成员作为编辑者。</p> <p>只邀请你信任、可以编辑网站代码和内容的人员。</p> <ol> <li>打开网站并选择 <strong>Share（分享）</strong>。</li> <li>在 <strong>Add people or groups（添加人员或群组）</strong>下查找并选择一名工作区成员。对方会先被添加为访客。</li> <li>在该人员旁边打开 <strong>Can view（可查看）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Can edit（可编辑）</strong>。访问权限会自动保存。此网站会显示在该成员 Sites 视图的 <strong>Shared with you（与你共享）</strong>下。</li> <li>网站编辑者可以打开网站、进行更改、保存版本，并在所有者首次发布网站后发布更新。</li> </ol> <p>网站所有者负责管理编辑权限，可以将现有访客提升为编辑者、将编辑者改为 <strong>Can view（可查看）</strong>，或移除其访问权限。协同编辑不需要单独的工作区权限开关。</p> <p>编辑者不能更改网站受众范围、邀请或移除其他人员、管理设置或分析数据，也不能转移所有权。编辑者也不能执行网站的首次发布；网站所有者必须先发布网站，编辑者才能发布后续更新。</p> <p>编辑权限与访客访问权限是分开的。上述步骤会先将人员添加为访客，再授予编辑权限。将访客提升为编辑者不会改变网站的受众范围设置。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"publish-and-share\">Publish and share</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Review your site before publishing it, then choose who can visit and who can help edit it.</p> <p><a id=\"review-and-share-your-site\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"review-before-you-share\">Review before you share</h2> <p>Before you share a site:</p> <ol> <li> <h3 id=\"try-the-site\">Try the site</h3> </li> <li>Review its content, generated text and images, links, uploaded files, forms, and interactive behavior.</li> <li>Test the site from the intended visitor experience, including its access and sign-in behavior.</li> </ol> <p>For a site built from a local project, also review the source changes and any database migrations in the Codex <a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">review pane</a>.</p> <ol> <li> <h3 id=\"check-data-and-access\">Check data and access</h3> </li> <li>Confirm that it doesn't expose confidential or sensitive information, secret values, or third-party content you don't have the right to share.</li> <li>Review features that collect personal information or other visitor content. Decide whether the site should collect, share, or publish that information.</li> <li>If the site uses Sign in with ChatGPT, explain what visitor information it receives and how it uses that information.</li> <li> <p>If the site collects or processes personal data, comply with <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001340\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">applicable privacy and data-protection laws (online)</a>.</p> </li> <li> <h3 id=\"choose-the-audience\">Choose the audience</h3> </li> <li>Choose the narrowest sharing option that fits the intended audience.</li> <li>Open the shared site and confirm that the intended audience can visit it.</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"control-access-and-secrets\"></a></p> <p>Keep access limited while you review the content, data handling, and expected audience.</p> <p>Use the sharing options shown for your site to choose who can visit. Visitor access lets people open the site; it doesn't give them editing access.</p> <p>For limited sharing, invited visitors must sign in with the account that received access. A public site is available without ChatGPT workspace access. A site's audience setting and any sign-in feature built into the site are separate controls.</p> <p>For sharing controls and site management instructions, see <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/articles/20001339\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Creating and managing ChatGPT sites (online)</a> in the Help Center.</p> <p><a id=\"update-your-site\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"publish-an-update\">Publish an update</h2> <p>Open your site in ChatGPT and describe the changes you want. Review the result, save a version, and deploy it. Check the changes at the published URL.</p> <p>Review the site code and any data the site saves or displays. Test the published site with an account from its intended audience.</p> <h2 id=\"choose-who-can-visit\">Choose who can visit</h2> <p>A new site is limited to its owner and workspace admins until you change its access. Depending on your account and workspace settings, the sharing options can include:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Owner and workspace admins</strong></li> <li><strong>Selected active users or groups</strong>, where supported</li> <li><strong>Invited external viewers</strong>, when external invitations are available</li> <li><strong>Anyone in the workspace</strong>, where supported</li> <li><strong>Anyone on the internet</strong>, only when public publishing is enabled</li> </ul> <p>In Enterprise workspaces, public publishing is off by default. An admin must enable it before eligible members can publish publicly. Visitor access lets someone open a site; it doesn't give them editing access. <a href=\"#/article/a-e62c8f8bdac9e5df?anchor=enable-sites-and-permissions\">See the Sites administration guide</a>.</p> <p>For example, you could ask:</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Change this site's access to everyone in my workspace after showing me the current site and confirming its URL.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"invite-people-outside-your-workspace\">Invite people outside your workspace</h2> <p>External invitations let you share a site with named viewers without making it public. You can invite people outside your workspace or share a private site from a personal account.</p> <p>External invitations are rolling out to sites users on Plus, Pro, Business, and Enterprise plans. If the invitation option is missing, check the selected account, site ownership, workspace permissions, and rollout availability.</p> <ol> <li>Open a site you own and select <strong>Share</strong>.</li> <li>To keep the site private, set <strong>Who has access</strong> to <strong>Only those invited</strong>.</li> <li>Enter the viewer's email address under <strong>Search for people or groups</strong>, or <strong>Enter an email address</strong> for a personal site, then select the recipient.</li> <li>Review the audience and the recipient's <strong>Viewer</strong> access, then select <strong>Invite</strong>.</li> <li>Confirm that the viewer appears in the saved access list. Share the site's link and ask them to sign in with the account that received access.</li> </ol> <p>External viewers can open and use the site. They don't become workspace members or site editors, and can't edit or publish the site. The invitation grants access to this site; review its content and connected data before sharing.</p> <p>In Enterprise, admins manage <strong>Allow members to invite external visitors to sites</strong> under <strong>Workspace settings &gt; Permissions &amp; roles</strong>. This permission is separate from permission to publish sites publicly. Business workspaces don't have a separate external-invitation toggle; sites must be enabled and the feature must be available to the account.</p> <p>To remove a viewer, open the site's sharing controls and remove their access. Also check the remaining audience settings: removing one invitation doesn't remove access the person has through public, workspace, or group sharing.</p> <h2 id=\"collaborate-on-a-site\">Collaborate on a site</h2> <p>Site collaboration requires a workspace. When the feature is available, a site owner can invite active members of the same workspace as editors.</p> <p>Invite only people you trust to edit the site's code and content.</p> <ol> <li>Open the site and select <strong>Share</strong>.</li> <li>Under <strong>Add people or groups</strong>, find and select a workspace member. They are added as a visitor.</li> <li>Open <strong>Can view</strong> next to that person and choose <strong>Can edit</strong>. Access saves automatically. The site appears under <strong>Shared with you</strong> in the member's sites view.</li> <li>The editor can open the site, make changes, save versions, and publish updates after the owner has published the site for the first time.</li> </ol> <p>The site owner manages editor access and can promote an existing visitor to editor, change an editor to <strong>Can view</strong>, or remove their access. Co-editing doesn't add a separate workspace permission toggle.</p> <p>Editors can't change the site's audience, invite or remove other people, manage settings or analytics, or transfer ownership. An editor also can't perform the site's first publish; the owner must publish the site before editors can publish later updates.</p> <p>Editor access is separate from visitor access. The steps above first add the person as a visitor, then grant editing access. Promoting a visitor to editor doesn't change the site's audience setting.</p>"};
